<title>FRANCE: U.S. main country of origin for Paris Feb 97.</title>
<headline>U.S. main country of origin for Paris Feb 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in February 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading countries of origin for ADP imports (in tonnes) in February 1997, with percentage change on February 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	 11,843  down  0.9pct</p>
<p> 2  India		    2,195  down  5.6</p>
<p> 3  Japan		    2,143  up   55.3</p>
<p> 4  Canada		   1,836  down 16.7</p>
<p> 5  UK			 1,523  up   37.2</p>
<p> 6  Germany		  1,295  up   28.4</p>
<p> 7  Hong Kong		1,197  down 13.7</p>
<p> 8  Thailand		 1,189  up   46.7</p>
<p> 9  Senegal		  1,015  up   16.9</p>
<p> 10 Italy			888  down  3.1</p>
<p> 11 Kenya			821  down  8.3</p>
<p> 12 French West Indies     736  up   17.8</p>
<p> 13 Singapore		  680  up   48.2</p>
<p> 14 Morocco		    658  down 27.2</p>
<p> 15 Argentina		  650  up   22.9</p>
<p> 16 Brazil		     591  up   24.9</p>
<p> 17 Mauritius		  520  up   15.5</p>
<p> 18 Switzerland		517  up   27.8</p>
<p> 19 Korea			461  up   16.8</p>
<p> 20 Egypt			440  up   44.1</p>
<p>    Total		   31,198</p>
<p>Overall February 1997 import traffic to CDG and Orly, totalled 43,068 tonnes, an increase of 5.6 percent on the same month the previous year ADP figures show. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
